From b5715521ecf44e00fd39bf7bf4b064c3f9230b99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:58:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): credit the sync thread's own
 repair-revision steps; count repair rounds

Hub, 2026-11-12 (t_01a1d02bf3e0d019): after #1461 credited a round's feed applies, the hub sync thread still ran
the full repair pass on 60 of 62 sampled rounds (~40% of its wall time). A 147 s read-only trace of the live
kanban_repair_revision (2027 steps, 123 changes) attributed the gaps: 1743 steps from refresh_remote_parents,
174 from lease_version/sync_version updates on one hub card every ~1.5 s (lease mirrors), 37 from
push acknowledgements (outbox deletes), all made by the sync thread after it read its repair inputs. Only feed
applies inside pull() were credited, so every round saw a gap.

kanban_sync_own_writes records, per board file, every revision step the sync thread makes through its live
connection inside credited(): pull, refresh_remote_parents, push and worker-placement reevaluate. The recorder is
a TEMP trigger gated by a connection function that answers only for the calling thread, so it never changes the
schema, commits and rolls back with the write, and ignores every other connection and thread (dispatcher,
heartbeats, workers, CLI): those writes stay gaps and repair at once. Steps drain to a per-file list when the
block ends outside a transaction, so a round on another pooled connection still chains them.

The window decision moves to kanban_sync_repair_window.decide, which returns why a pass ran (first, unknown,
rebuilt, inputs, local_write, window) or deferred. note_round counts unchanged/deferred/full-pass rounds per
board and logs them at INFO every 10 minutes ("kanban sync: <board> repair rounds in Ns: ..."), so live
verification no longer needs py-spy --locals.

Tests: the push-ack case now defers (it was pinned as a gap); new unit tests for the recorder (other thread,
other connection, rollback, mid-transaction, no revision table) and round tests (reservation write credited,
another thread's write during the round still repairs, counter/log line, decide reasons).
